davisongeorge@gmail.com wrote:
[Work and home comp problems]
> I have hearse installed on both and it syncs after each game if the
> internet is available. If a bone file has been synced from the other
> computer hearse reports a collision and doesn't check it in. This is
> kind of annoying since without this hearse just checks its internal
> database and doesn't connect. I wish it would update internally if it
> found the file online.

Hearse keeps track of the last date it was run and tries to upload any 
bones file newer than that.

Here's my suggestion, which you can probably automate in some sexy way.

<presync>
Computer A: hearse
Computer B: hearse
<now both have uploaded any bones files they've got>
<sync>
Computer A: hearse /r
Computer B: hearse /r

The /r switch tells Hearse to update the 'last run' timestamp to *now* 
and exit without doing any more work.  Now both comps have uploaded any 
new bones files they've got since the last sync and are up to date.

The alternative is simply to ignore the warning message :)

